We establish the non-Archimedean and p-adic Banach space counterparts to the Welch bounds recently derived by M. Krishna. Specifically, we demonstrate the following results:

1. Let $\mathbb{K}$ be a complete non-Archimedean valued field where $\left|\sum_{j=1}^{n}\lambda_j^2\right|=\max_{1\leq j \leq n}|\lambda_j|^2$ holds for all $\lambda_j \in \mathbb{K}$ and $n \in \mathbb{N}$. Consider a $d$-dimensional non-Archimedean Banach space $\mathcal{X}$ over $\mathbb{K}$. Given any collections $\{\tau_j\}_{j=1}^n$ in $\mathcal{X}$ and $\{f_j\}_{j=1}^n$ in $\mathcal{X}^*$ (the dual space) such that $f_j(\tau_j) =1$ for all $1\leq j \leq n$, if the operator $S_{f, \tau} : \text{Sym}^m(\mathcal{X})\ni x \mapsto \sum_{j=1}^nf_j^{\otimes m}(x)\tau_j^{\otimes m}$ is diagonalizable, then:
\begin{align} \text{(Non-Archimedean Functional Welch Bounds)} \quad
\max_{1\leq j,k \leq n, j \neq k}\{|n|, |f_j(\tau_k)f_k(\tau_j)|^{m} \}\geq
\frac{|n|^2}{\left|{d+m-1 \choose m}\right| }. \end{align}

2. For a prime $p$, let $\mathbb{Q}_p$ denote the p-adic number field. Let $\mathcal{X}$ be a $d$-dimensional p-adic Banach space over $\mathbb{Q}_p$. If $\{\tau_j\}_{j=1}^n$ is a collection in $\mathcal{X}$ and $\{f_j\}_{j=1}^n$ is a collection in $\mathcal{X}^*$ satisfying $f_j(\tau_j) =1$ for all $1\leq j \leq n$, and there exists a scalar $b \in \mathbb{Q}_p$ such that $\sum_{j=1}^{n}f_j^{\otimes m}(x) \tau_j^{\otimes m} =bx$ for every $x \in \text{Sym}^m(\mathcal{X})$, then:
\begin{align} \text{(p-adic Functional Welch Bounds)} \quad \max_{1\leq j,k \leq n, j \neq k}\{|n|,
|f_j(\tau_k)f_k(\tau_j)|^{m} \}\geq \frac{|n|^2}{\left|{d+m-1 \choose m}\right|
}. \end{align}

Furthermore, we formulate the non-Archimedean and p-adic functional versions of the Zauner conjecture.

